.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
*.log

# Real ERP export and everything derived from it. Customer names, Riviera PO
# numbers, sales orders, hull numbers and internal notes — Stella's and
# Riviera's order book. Never commit these; the repo is public.
# The files live on disk for local test runs; originals are in ../handoff/.
tests/fixtures/

# The vessel code map: every boat, its Stella and Riviera codes, its hull
# prefixes and the item codes built for it. It is Stella's and Riviera's product
# structure and it was being served as a plain JSON file to anyone who asked.
#
# It is only ever a BOOTSTRAP — `loadCodes` seeds Firestore from it once, and
# from then on Firestore is the source of truth. A deployment that has been
# seeded never reads it again, so the live app does not need it and the
# repository should not carry it. The file lives in the private handoff folder.
data/vessel-codes.seed.json

# The test suite lives with the data it tests.
#
# Every assertion is written against the real export — real vessel codes, real
# item codes, real hull numbers, and at one point a real customer's name. The
# fixtures were already private, which made the tests unrunnable for anybody
# else anyway, so the file was carrying that exposure for no benefit.
#
# It sits in the private handoff folder, next to the fixtures. Copy it back into
# tests/ to run it; do not commit it.
tests/
